Relevant columns and their potential usage for the task  
• station_id : uniquely identifies each bike‑share station – use COUNT(DISTINCT station_id)  
• status      : tells whether a station record is flagged as 'active' or 'closed' – use in a WHERE / GROUP BY clause  
• modified_date : last time the row was changed – use EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) to assign a record to 2013 or 2014  

Typical conditions we will need  
• status IN ('active','closed')                                    -- keep only the two requested states  
• EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) IN (2013,2014)                  -- focus on the two years  
• GROUP BY EXTRACT(YEAR …), status                                 -- to get the two counts for each year  

Ten step‑by‑step investigation queries (LIMIT 20 on the exploratory ones)  
```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few station rows
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Which distinct status values exist?
SELECT DISTINCT status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Which years appear in modified_date?
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count distinct stations by status overall
SELECT status,
       COUNT(DISTINCT station_id) AS num_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
GROUP BY status
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Distinct stations per year (all statuses)
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) AS yr,
       COUNT(DISTINCT station_id)        AS num_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) IN (2013,2014)
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Distinct stations for 2013‑2014 but only active/closed
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) AS yr,
       status,
       COUNT(DISTINCT station_id)        AS num_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status IN ('active','closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) IN (2013,2014)
GROUP BY yr,status
ORDER BY yr,status
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Detailed counts for 2013
SELECT status,
       COUNT(DISTINCT station_id) AS num_stations_2013
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status IN ('active','closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) = 2013
GROUP BY status
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Detailed counts for 2014
SELECT status,
       COUNT(DISTINCT station_id) AS num_stations_2014
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status IN ('active','closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) = 2014
GROUP BY status
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Pivot the counts so active & closed are columns (2013‑2014)
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date)                     AS yr,
       COUNT(DISTINCT IF(status = 'active', station_id, NULL)) AS active_stations,
       COUNT(DISTINCT IF(status = 'closed', station_id, NULL)) AS closed_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status IN ('active','closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) IN (2013,2014)
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: number of distinct active & closed stations for 2013 and 2014
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date)                       AS year,
  COUNT(DISTINCT IF(status = 'active', station_id, NULL)) AS active_station_count,
  COUNT(DISTINCT IF(status = 'closed', station_id, NULL)) AS closed_station_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status IN ('active','closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM modified_date) IN (2013,2014)
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year;
```

